# Editor and tool state — local to a machine, never part of the site.
.obsidian/
.claude/

# FreeFileSync writes one HTML session log per mirror run. Diagnostics, not
# history — the dated one-liner in logs/mirror_log.md is the record.
logs/mirror-ffs/

# Bill and Cowork work on alphas here while a Claude Code session is running in
# the repo. Untracked on purpose: it keeps in-progress design out of the history
# and out of any `git add -A`, so the two can work without colliding.
prep/

# Staging is created outside the repo, but belt and braces.
.pull-staging/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.workroot/

# `build-finance-page.py` writes a per-place {ISO3}-summary.csv on every build, and
# nothing reads it: budget work is suspended, so `country.py` does not open it and
# `finance.py` does not aggregate it. Bill removed all 59 from the repo on 2026-08-14
# for that reason; the compiler keeps producing them, so they are ignored rather than
# deleted in a loop. Drop this line when budget work resumes.
outputs/non-state-finance/*-summary.csv

# The index is rebuildable scaffolding and is never committed — the freshness
# sweep in vault_lib is what pays for that. Corpus reads OSINT's through the
# workroot junctions; an index/ appearing here means a script was run with the
# repo root as ROOT, which indexes a tree holding none of the roots and yields
# a correct index of nothing. That state reports itself *fresh*, so nothing
# rebuilds and nothing warns. Committed once on 2026-08-14 (c53dcf7); removed.
index/
